emanding work  environment Pincus had heard it all  before I think Mark doesn't suffer fools  DreamWorks Animation CEO Jeffrey  Katzenberg sits on Zynga's board of  directors and it's as simple as that and  what he has is a very high regard in  admiration for smart talented people who  deliver and if you'd are not that then  he doesn't have a lot of patience so  maybe that's why we're buddies Zynga's  IPO is said to be the biggest u.s. web  one since Google Zynga went public in  December 2011 with a 7 billion dollar  valuation and with Pincus retaining  unprecedented voting power but Pincus  couldn't control what happened next its  first quarter earnings report in 2012  showed that the company was spending  more and more on R&amp;D and spending more  and more for each game that it was  putting out and users were not staying  is in fact it was saying to investors  that a majority of its growth was coming  in mobile games which was not where it  was spending majority of its R&amp;D dollars  the growth on the web slowed down you  know it kind of stalled the transition  to mobile surprised us as it seems to be  surprised in the whole world eight  months after its initial public offering  the company had lost over 70% of its  value and there was more bad news to  come another top executive is leaving  Zynga several key executives left and  the company was hit with lawsuits for  copyright infringement  and insider trading and the fragile  relationship between Facebook and Zynga  showed signs of unraveling its next big  fall came in the wake of Facebook's IPO  bazinga relies almost exclusively on  Facebook for its fourths revenue and  Facebook's IPO was a big fizzle that in  turn dragged Zynga down along with it  Zynga just cut its earnings forecast for  both the third quarter and the full-year  quote the third quarter of 2012  continued to be challenging and while  many of our games performed as planned  as a whole we did not execute to our  satisfaction end quote  despit